--- /dev/null
+++ b/llvm/test/tools/llvm-profgen/Inputs/ip-mode/gnu-thumb/README.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+GNU AS Thumb DWARF addresses (patch 8)
+GNU AS 2.43, GBS armv7l emul tools; GNU ld 2.43.
+Commands run here with the GBS loader/library path:
+  as -g -o <temp>/gnu-thumb.o gnu-thumb.s
+  ld --build-id=sha1 -e gnu_thumb -Ttext=0x1000 -o gnu-thumb.perfbin <temp>/gnu-thumb.o
+Natural DWARF subprogram [0x1001,0x1009); CU [0x1000,0x1008).
+Known instructions from source: 0x1000 movs (2), 0x1002 add.w (4), 0x1006 bx (2).
+.text file offset=VA=0x1000. Bit-zero normalization yields [0x1000,0x1008).
+Negative derived files (LLVM objcopy 22.1.8):
+  llvm-objcopy --redefine-sym='$t=$a' gnu-thumb.perfbin odd-arm.perfbin
+  llvm-objcopy --redefine-sym='$t=$d' gnu-thumb.perfbin odd-data.perfbin
+  llvm-objcopy --dump-section=.debug_info=<temp>/debug-info.bin gnu-thumb.perfbin
+  Change little-endian uint32 at section offset 0x2c from 0x1001 to 0x1005.
+  llvm-objcopy --update-section=.debug_info=<temp>/middle-debug-info.bin gnu-thumb.perfbin odd-middle.perfbin
+The negative mapping/range edits are intentionally inconsistent metadata, not compiler outputs.
+odd-middle clears to 0x1004, inside add.w; odd-arm/data must not normalize.
+All samples are synthetic; no sampled PC is cleared.
+
+Adjacent GNU AS case: as -g -o <temp>/adjacent.o adjacent.s;
+ld --build-id=sha1 -e first -Ttext=0x1000 -o adjacent.perfbin <temp>/adjacent.o.
+first [0x1001,0x1005), second [0x1005,0x1009); instruction starts 1000,1002,1004,1006.
+The second normalized start 0x1004 is inside the first raw DWARF range.
+line-mismatch.perfbin: SYNTHETIC DWARF2 line metadata; minimum_instruction_length=1,
+set_address 0x1000, advance_line +8, copy (line9); advance_pc 1,
+advance_line +1, copy (line10); advance_pc 7, end_sequence.
+Replace only .debug_line using llvm-objcopy --update-section=.debug_line=<temp>/synthetic-line.bin.
+This intentionally impossible instruction-level line split tests alias consistency failure;
+it is not a compiler-produced line table. Complete generator lives in alias-fixtures.py
+in the project evidence; lit only reads the resulting ELF.
